    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0304" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.13/30.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is a movement to secure the pardon of Asbert alone, through amnesty
                    proceedings, the contention being that Arias admitted killing Rivas and there is
                    no doubt of Asbert’s guilt. I assume Department is not interested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
